instruction: Given a string, convert it to uppercase and replace vowels with corresponding numbers. For example, "Hello World" becomes "HELLO WORLD".

response: Here is the solution:

```java
public class StringManipulator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String input = "Hello World";
        String output = input.toUpperCase();

        // Replace vowels with corresponding numbers
        String vowelMap = "AEIOUaeiou";
        String result = "";

        for (int i = 0; i < output.length(); i++) {
            char c = output.charAt(i);
            if (vowelMap.indexOf(c) != -1) {
                result += (vowelMap.indexOf(c) + 1) + "";
            } else {
                result += c;
            }
        }

        System.out.println(result);
    }
}
```
In this solution, we first convert the input string to uppercase. Then, we iterate through each character in the string and check if it is a vowel. If it is, we replace it with the corresponding number based on its position in the vowel map. Finally, we print the modified string.

